  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 247 AM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nA shortwave trough lifting out of the Southwest will keep some mid-\nlevel clouds over much of the area today-tonight which could impact \nforecast high temperatures this afternoon. There is higher \nconfidence that will will see some light shower activity and \nsprinkles lingering across much of the area today through tonight. \nAn isolated thunderstorm will be hard to rule out tonight with some \nsteepening mid-lvl lapse rates and elevated cape around 250 J/KG as \nthe shortwave trough pivots across the area. Strong or severe storms \nare NOT expected.\n\nWed-Thu...Cloudiness may linger into Wed but the probabilities for \nlight showers/sprinkles are expected to subside as the \nmid/upper ridge begins to amplify over the area once again \nbringing seasonably mild temperatures with highs in the low to \nmid 70s. Another mild day is anticipated on Thu with a compact \nridge situated over the area while a more vigorous mid/upper \ntrough moves over the Great Basin area impacting the Central \nRockies.\n\nThis trough is progged to translate slowly eastward into the Rockies \nFri-Sat keeping the higher probabilities for showers just west of \nthe area. By late Sunday, this trough is progged to emerge from the \nRockies bringing increasing chances for showers to the area Sun into \nMon while a cold front users in cooler but seasonable air for the \nstart of the next week.",
